SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] BNC Notice & Service Disruption
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, October 15\, 2026\nThe Bankruptcy Noticing Center (
 BNC) has been experiencing a nationwide service disruption since on or abo
 ut October 9\, 2026\, affecting all U.S. Bankruptcy Courts. The outage has
  interrupted the BNC's processing and delivery of notices and orders issue
 d by the Court. As a result\, parties who ordinarily receive notices and o
 rders through the BNC may experience delays in receiving those documents. 
 The outage is also affecting CM/ECF users' ability to generate and print a
  List of Creditors.\nThe outage does not affect the electronic delivery of
  Notices of Electronic Filing (NEFs)\, which continue to be generated and 
 distributed normally through CM/ECF.\nAt this time\, there is no estimated
  date or time for restoration of services.\nAdditionally\, the following w
 ebsites are unavailable:\nbnc.uscourts.gov\nbankruptcynotices.uscourts.gov
 \nnotices.uscourts.gov\nNational Creditor Registration Service website tha
 t supports CM/ECF access to address labels\nThe Court will provide additio
 nal updates as information becomes available.\nhttps://www.meb.uscourts.go
 v/news/bnc-notice-service-disruption
URL:https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/bnc-notice-service-disruption
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
